WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language:  en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:06.160
There is no single character that represents
One Piece as well as the man, the woman, the

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:09.250
myth, the legend: Bon Kurei.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:13.809
No matter what we thought upon our first impressions
in Alabasta, there isn’t a One Piece fan

00:00:13.809 --> 00:00:19.990
out there that didn’t fall in love with
Bentham / Mr. 2 Bon Kurei- a character with

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.960
seemingly as many names as faces.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:29.950
At least, I can’t comprehend someone seeing
Bentham’s multiple heroic sacrifices and

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:35.870
not weeping over the true power of friendship
that he demonstrates.

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:40.900
You see, Bon Kurei *is* One Piece.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:41.900
…

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:42.900
The series, not the treasure.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:47.079
That would be the plot twist to end all plot
twists.

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:53.270
No, what we should say is that Bentham embodies
what One Piece is as a series.

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:59.450
So, today we’re going to talk about Un,
Deux, Trois ways that this character demonstrates

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:03.649
some of the story’s most important traits
and themes.

00:01:03.649 --> 00:01:10.719
**First, Bentham is a wacky character who
delivers a huge emotional impact.**

00:01:10.719 --> 00:01:14.960
If there are two barriers to entry for new
One Piece readers, they’re the series’

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.310
length and Oda’s art style.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:24.710
However, while 1,000 chapters seems daunting
at first, once readers are caught up, they’ll

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:28.020
learn the truth: One Piece is *not* too long.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.850
It’s actually too short.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:33.100
But if you’re watching this channel, you
probably already know that.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:37.909
What we should talk about instead is the other
complaint we might hear from people hesitant

00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:41.310
to come along for the voyage - Oda’s art
style.

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:48.280
Compared to edgier, darker looking Shonen
like Bleach or Naruto, One Piece looks positively

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:49.280
cartoonish.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:55.310
In fact, Eiichiro Oda’s character designs
look rather unique within the world of manga

00:01:55.310 --> 00:02:01.990
as a whole - he has a style all his own that
looks more Bugs Bunny than Berserk.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:07.429
People are often initially put off by this
art style, claiming it looks too silly or

00:02:07.429 --> 00:02:08.429
unserious.

00:02:08.429 --> 00:02:13.540
But what these readers don’t yet realize
is that that silliness is one of One Piece’s

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:15.280
greatest strengths.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:20.959
One Piece *is* silly - it’s goofy and ridiculous
- it’s genuinely funny and will make you

00:02:20.959 --> 00:02:23.840
laugh out loud again and again.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:29.019
But one of the beautiful things about that
comic tone is that it makes the deeper emotional

00:02:29.019 --> 00:02:32.090
beats hit that much harder.

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:35.000
The humor disarms us - we let our guard down.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:39.900
Then, because we’re initially just along
for a silly pirate adventure, the audience

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:45.489
is reduced to tears when we learn that our
crew mates have the saddest backstories known

00:02:45.489 --> 00:02:46.489
to man.

00:02:46.489 --> 00:02:47.489
This blue-nosed reindeer?

00:02:47.489 --> 00:02:49.440
He will make you cry.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:51.489
This speedo-wearing cyborg?

00:02:51.489 --> 00:02:53.470
*He* will make you cry.

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:54.799
This skeleton with an afro?

00:02:54.799 --> 00:02:58.530
Yes, even he will make you cry.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:04.060
Bentham functions as a perfect example of
this phenomenon.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:09.879
When we first meet Bon-Chan, it’s as Mr.
2 Bon Kurei - an agent of Crocodile’s Baroque

00:03:09.879 --> 00:03:10.879
Works organization.

00:03:10.879 --> 00:03:15.379
By the way, while I was researching for this
video I learned something that…wow, I feel

00:03:15.379 --> 00:03:17.620
like I should have known all along.

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:22.810
Even though we often refer to Bentham as Bon-Clay
as if that’s their name, it turns out that

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:27.879
Bon Kurei actually refers to a specific night
in the Japanese Obon Festival.

00:03:27.879 --> 00:03:33.800
So, whereas most of the Baroque Works agents
feature male and female pairs with the man

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:39.310
being named after a number and the woman being
named after a holiday, I.e., Mr. 3 and Miss

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:42.659
Goldenweek or Mr. 4 and Miss Merry Christmas.

00:03:42.659 --> 00:03:49.260
Bentham, however, being genderfluid has both
code names.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:54.590
Surprisingly progressive for Sir Crocodile…or
not very surprising if we accept the Croco-Mom

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:55.590
theory.

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:58.810
And as a quick note before we get into the
rest of the video, we’re using he/him pronouns

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:03.459
for Bentham since those are what are used
in the manga and anime, but it is important

00:04:03.459 --> 00:04:08.200
to note that the character has referred to
himself as a man and a woman.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:14.889
But back to how Bentham exemplifies a wacky
character with hard hitting emotional impact.

00:04:14.889 --> 00:04:20.220
When we first meet Mr. 2 Bon Kurei, the audience
is struck by possibly the most ridiculous

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:23.440
character design in the series up to that
point.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:29.620
He’s a drowning ballerina adorned with massive
“2” shaped swans and a make-up job worse

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:30.620
than Buggy’s.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:37.090
Especially in the anime, the over-the-top
drama in every one of his lines is masterfully

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:43.750
performed by voice actor Kazuki Yao - a performer
whose energy is so unmatched he would eventually

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:47.560
be welcomed into the crew proper as the voice
of Franky.

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:52.350
He’s relegated to such a position of comic
relief all throughout this scene and the remainder

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:57.690
of Alabasta, that we can hardly predict it
coming when in the end of the arc, he disguises

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:03.140
himself and his crew as the Straw Hats so
that the real Straw Hats can evade capture

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:04.280
by the Marines.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:11.190
All along, Mr. 2 has been espousing the power
of true friendship in an exaggerated, melodramatic

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:18.080
manner, but suddenly when the crew’s livelihood
is on the line, it’s Bentham who puts his

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:25.730
money where his mouth is in a moment of complete
sacrifice.

00:05:25.730 --> 00:05:32.410
Seeing such goofy characters deliver on powerful
emotional moments is one of the touchstones

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:36.840
of One Piece, and Bon Kurei is emblematic
of this feature.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:43.000
**Secondly, Bon-Chan is representative of
one of One Piece’s central themes: Friendship.**

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:48.300
There’s a good reason that so many Western
fans know the word nakama - “companion”

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:49.800
or “friend.”

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:54.090
During Bentham’s first meeting with the
straw hats, they become fast friends.

00:05:54.090 --> 00:06:00.160
Mr. 2 and his entertaining copy ability mesmerizes
the more “immature” crew mates - Luffy,

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:01.560
Usopp, and Chopper.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:08.150
In fact, they slot in so well with each other
that they immediately become lifelong friends.

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:13.080
However, once the crew realized that Bentham
was in fact an agent of Baroque Works who

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:18.150
now possessed the ability to change into any
of their crew at will, the Straw Hats devised

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:20.060
a countermeasure against this technique.

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:25.630
They drew X’s on their wrists and then covered
them by tying a bandage around the X.

00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:31.310
What at first was a clever way to defend against
Mr. 2’s devil fruit power set the groundwork

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:35.740
for one of the most emotional moments of the
Alabasta saga.

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:39.310
These X’s allowed for their silent goodbye
to Vivi.

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:43.410
While they couldn’t risk revealing their
close connection to the princess to the Marines,

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:48.740
raising these marks into the air allowed them
to demonstrate their bonds to one another,

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:51.680
signifying their undying friendship.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:55.400
Before this, when the Marines are in heavy
pursuit of the Straw Hats, they’re able

00:06:55.400 --> 00:07:01.640
to escape Black Cage Hina when Mr. 2 disguises
his ship and crew as the Straw Hats, acting

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:02.640
as decoys.

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:07.650
Even though sailing to meet Vivi at the rendezvous
point will put them directly in the path of

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:12.800
the Marines, Bon Kurei sacrifices himself
and his crew in order to give them the chance

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:16.840
to say farewell to their friend.

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:22.530
Bon Clay has a power that seems inherently
deceitful - he uses it to impersonate Nefertari

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:27.140
Cobra and kick off a war in Alabasta as part
of Crocodile’s plan.

00:07:27.140 --> 00:07:30.140
Posing as someone else has its roots in subterfuge
and trickery.

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:36.200
We see this especially in its former user,
Higurashi, who used it to fool Oden into thinking

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:41.740
Momonosuke was in danger, allowing Kaidou
to make the finishing blow in their battle.

00:07:41.740 --> 00:07:47.900
However, in Bentham’s sacrifice, we see
the nature of the fruit subverted.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:54.840
He’s still using the Mane Mane no Mi to
trick someone - in this case Hina - but for

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:59.870
the greater good of allowing his friends to
continue their adventure.

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:05.760
Mr. 2 Bon Kurei is one of the first of Luffy’s
enemies who’s turned into a friend.

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:11.640
As Mihawk thought at Marineford, Luffy’s
most dangerous ability is turning those around

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:12.780
him into allies.

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:19.120
In Impel Down, the second arc to heavily feature
Bentham, this trait of Luffy’s is exemplified.

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:24.130
What began in Alabasta with Mr. 2 rallying
to Luffy’s aid became an entire rag-tag

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:29.400
crew of Luffy’s former enemies becoming
invaluable allies.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:34.520
Even Bon Kurei’s former employer, Crocodile,
would join Luffy’s side in the Paramount

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:35.520
War.

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:41.430
And once again, Bentham would make an ultimate
sacrifice for the sake of friendship, allowing

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:46.370
everyone to escape the impenetrable prison
of Impel Down.

00:08:46.370 --> 00:08:51.970
You know, speaking of Crocodile: he has an
81,000,000 bounty.

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:54.700
Since I have around 580,000 subscribers.

00:08:54.700 --> 00:09:00.670
- if we converted that into dollars and then
converted *those* into berries, I would have

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:03.050
a 59,000,000 berry bounty.

00:09:03.050 --> 00:09:07.900
Making me significantly less dangerous than
this slimy man right here.

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:13.010
So please help me change that by subscribing
to the channel and raising my bounty!

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:19.140
**The third and final way that Bon Kurei embodies
the themes of One PIece is by representing

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:24.180
the absolute freedom that Luffy seeks to bring
to the world.**

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:29.940
If there’s one theme that echoes through
the series even more powerfully than that

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:33.240
of friendship, it is the theme of freedom.

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:38.420
Luffy wants to become the Pirate King - the
person with the most freedom on the sea.

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:43.940
Nearly every island that the Straw Hats travel
to, they restore freedom to the citizens.

00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:51.250
Like Joyboy before him, Luffy’s heart beats
in time with the drums of liberation.

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:56.040
The Okama Way is also a way of freedom.

00:09:56.040 --> 00:10:01.420
In Bentham’s great sacrifice at Impel Down,
he grants the prisoners who allied with Luffy

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:02.880
freedom from the prison.

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:15.529
However, he also represents this theme to
the core of his 

00:10:15.529 --> 00:11:03.650
very being: as an Okama.

00:11:03.650 --> 00:11:20.150
It’s no coincidence that Emporio Ivankov
and the Kamabakka Kingdom are aligned with

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:21.580
the Revolutionary Army.

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:26.780
Monkey D. Dragon opposes the authoritarian
rule of the World Government and the Celestial

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:27.780
Dragons.

00:11:27.780 --> 00:11:34.440
With him, opposing this fascistic force, are
representatives of the oppressed people of

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:35.670
the One Piece world.

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:40.890
Bartholomew Kuma, who literally had his agency
stripped away to become a slave to the Celestial

00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:47.220
Dragons; The Fishman Hack and Koala, representing
the Fishmen who are relegated to live beneath

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:52.970
the red line, away from the sunlight of the
surface; and Emporio Ivankov, ruler of the

00:11:52.970 --> 00:11:57.500
Okama - the LGBT community of the One Piece
world.

00:11:57.500 --> 00:12:01.750
In our real world, queer communities have
fought long and hard for decades against brutal

00:12:01.750 --> 00:12:07.550
discrimination in order to be free to express
themselves and be able to love who they love.

00:12:07.550 --> 00:12:13.570
And it’s the same in One Piece for figures
like Ivankov who allies himself with the Revolutionary

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:20.630
Army. (which, like, *come on Sanji*, you clearly
have some internalized prejudices you need

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:22.010
to work through).

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:26.380
From the moment we meet Bentham, he is unabashedly
who he wants to be.

00:12:26.380 --> 00:12:29.050
He puts no limits on his self-expression.

00:12:29.050 --> 00:12:30.610
He dresses the way he wants to.

00:12:30.610 --> 00:12:34.410
He applies makeup the way he wants to.

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:37.360
He identifies fluidly with the gender that
he wants to.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:42.560
His Clone-Clone fruit even lets him literally
become whoever he wants to.

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:47.300
This absolute freedom of expression and gender
is an extension of the freedom that Straw

00:12:47.300 --> 00:12:53.880
Hat Luffy fights to bring to the world - one
of the central goals and themes of the entire

00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:54.880
series.

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:59.450
Now, remaining in Impel Down, Bon-Chan is
the new Queen of Newkama Land.

00:12:59.450 --> 00:13:04.210
As he says during his sacrifice in Alabasta,
“one may stray from the path of man.

00:13:04.210 --> 00:13:06.620
One may stray from the path of woman.

00:13:06.620 --> 00:13:09.470
But there is no straying from the path of
humanity.”

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:11.540
This is the Okama Way.

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:15.750
Or maybe Ivankov has already come to break
him out with the help of Luffy’s father.

00:13:15.750 --> 00:13:20.130
And if you want to learn more about Monkey
D. Dragon and who he truly is, you really

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:22.750
can’t skip this video here.

